{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>I will go down now.</b> This teaches the judges that they must not decide capital cases except by direct inspection — all as I explained in the section of the Dispersion. Another interpretation: I will go down to the end of their deeds." "<b>Her cry.</b> Of the whole province." "<b>Which has come to Me — they have done.</b> And if they persist in their rebellion — I will make an end of them. And if they do not persist in rebellion — I will know what to do, to exact payment from them through suffering and not make an end of them. And its parallel we find elsewhere: ״וְעַתָּה הוֹרֵד עֶדְיְךָ מֵעָלֶיךָ וְאֵדְעָה מָה אֶעֱשֶׂה לָּךְ״ (Exodus 33). And therefore there is a paseq break between עָשׂוּ and כָלָה, to separate one word from its fellow. And our Sages interpreted הַכְּצַעֲקָתָהּ — the cry of one girl whom they killed by an extraordinary death because she gave food to a poor person, as explained in its place."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:20.507704034Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}